- op: discuss  # 457f
  at: '2026-08-31T23:27:25Z'  # 457f
  by: agent  # 457f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 457f
  clock: 4  # 457f
  nonce: 457f  # 457f
  message: "SECOND DELIVERABLE SHIPPED (dev e66ab343a3), and it CLOSED INV-fumod shape (b).\nOf the three gaps this item named, two are done and one remains.\n\nDONE: per-name pairing (`_source_names_can_reach_sink`) and the fetch rule\n(`_FAR_SIDE_FETCH_COMMANDS`). Live on INV-fumod's own instance, cold:\nviolated(6) -> violated(3), filed row gone. Cohort, 15 repos, all cold: 19 rows\nremoved, 0 new findings, no verdict changed category.\n\nREMAINS: cross-`source` name reach, now filed as its own invariant INV-pujob\nwith a live instance attached (guacamole's DESTINATION, assigned at\nbuild-guacamole.sh:58 and read as an environment variable because it is never\nassigned in the file that uses it).\n\nTWO THINGS THE FIRST DELIVERABLE'S NOTE GOT WRONG, corrected here rather than\nleft standing:\n  1. It said per-name pairing \"requires the taint engine to pair on the source\n     edge's env_var ... which it does not do -- all bash env reads collapse to\n     one env.environ source symbol\". The collapse is real but the NAMES are\n     not lost: when collapsed sites disagree, ir._absorb_per_call_site_key\n     moves them to `env_var_values`. Reading only the singular is what loses\n     them, and that was my first implementation.\n  2. It described the gate as belonging in the structural propagator. bash\n     reaches findings through the DDG arm, which reports analysis_method\n     \"structural\" with walk_verdict \"unavailable\" when no DDG exists. Gating\n     one arm left INV-fumod's instance standing with every unit test green.\n     Both arms are now gated and both are pinned."  # 457f
